---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="FAQ">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">FAQ</h1>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-6">
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Is the AI information reliable?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        Treat it as a starting point. Every page carries an unverified banner until community
        editors have confirmed its contents, field-level confidence is shown where applicable,
        and the original document is always one click away.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Who can edit?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        Any signed-in user can propose edits. New proposals are reviewed by moderators;
        trusted editors (5+ accepted edits) publish instantly.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Can I submit agreements in any language?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        Yes. The AI reads the original language and writes the summary in English.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">How do I find a specific provision?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        <a href="/agreements/" class="underline">Browse</a> searches titles, summaries and the
        full text of every submitted document, and filters by country and sector. Searches are
        linkable — copy the URL to share one.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">What if the source link dies?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        Where a document was uploaded rather than pasted, we keep an archived copy and link it
        from the agreement page alongside the original source.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">How do I keep an eye on edits?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        <a href="/changes" class="underline">Recent changes</a> lists every published revision,
        and each agreement has a full history showing exactly what each edit changed. There is
        also an <a href="/changes.xml" class="underline">Atom feed</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Are these documents copyrighted?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">
        Rules differ by jurisdiction; many agreements are public filings. We host only publicly
        available documents, link the source for every one, and honour takedown requests from
        rights holders.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Is this legal advice?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-stone-700">No.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
